{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WzYkXVMvS4oPU3f413eexN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to go through each experiment that has status \"planned\" and predict what the results would look like if the best-case scenario holds.\n\nLet me also check the currently RUNNING experiments, as those are also pending results.\n\nLet me identify all experiments that are not DONE:\n\n**Planned experiments:**\n- exp-002: sica_k_ablation_14b (K sensitivity on D012 60 questions, Qwen-14B)\n- exp-003: tiebreak_baseline_analysis (already done as CPU analysis, noted in plan)\n\n\n- exp-006: c0_diagnostic_validation\n- exp-008: constraint_quality_case_studies\n\nNow I'm scanning through the registry to see which experiments are already completed or failed, filtering out the ones that don't need predictions.\n\nLooking at the currently running experiments across different model configurations and parameter settings, and there are a few queued ones waiting to start.\n\nNow I'm checking the experiment plan against the registry to see which ones marked as \"planned\" are actually complete or still need to run. Most of the earlier experiments through exp-019 are already done, with exp-051 currently executing. I need to identify which planned experiments still need detailed predicted data generated under the best tier. I'm seeing that many experiments marked as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan are actually already completed in the registry, so I need to clarify what the user is asking for—whether they want predictions for all planned experiments regardless of completion status, or just the ones that haven't been run yet. The core task seems to be generating detailed predictions for planned experiments that align with the \"best\" tier definition, but I should